[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Italian Game"]
[Variation "Rousseau Gambit"]
[ECO "C50"]
[Character "gambit,sharp"]
[Risk "high"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "trap,pawn-grab"]
[Themes "f-file-pressure,quick-development"]
[Kind "main"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 f5 { The Rousseau Gambit: Black offers the e-pawn to open the f-file against White's king. The engine thinks Black is about a pawn down, so play it as a surprise, not as best play. }
4. d3 { White's best answer. It guards e4 and refuses the gambit, and Black's own f-pawn move has left a hole in front of the king. } 4... Nf6 { Develops and hits e4 a second time. Black wants ...fxe4 whenever dxe4 would open lines for the black pieces. }
5. O-O ( 5. exf5? { Takes the pawn but gives up the centre and the e4 pawn that held Black back. } 5... d5 { Hits the bishop and shuts its diagonal, so ...Bxf5 wins the pawn back and Black has the better centre. } 6. Bb3 Bxf5 )
( 5. Ng5 5... d5 { Blocks the bishop's diagonal to f7 and hits it. Not 5...fxe4, which loses to Nf7 (see the trap Nf7 fork). } 6. exd5 Na5 { Attacks the bishop on c4 before it can use the pin on f7 or the diagonal to the king. } 7. Bb5+ c6 { Blocks the check with a pawn that also kicks the bishop. } 8. dxc6 bxc6 9. Ba4 Bd6 { Develops and puts the bishop on a diagonal toward White's king. } )
5... Bc5 { Aims at f2, the pawn that guards White's king, and gets Black ready to castle. }
6. Nc3 ( 6. exf5 6... d5 { Hits the bishop again and plans ...Bxf5, so the pawn comes back. } 7. Bb5 O-O { Castles at once: the king is safe and the rook already looks along the f-file. } 8. Bxc6 bxc6 9. Nxe5 Bxf5 )
6... d6 { Props up e5 and opens the road for the c8 bishop, while ...fxe4 stays in reserve. }
7. Bg5 7... Na5 { Challenges the bishop on c4, White's best attacker, before it can help Bg5 and Nd5 pile onto f6. }
8. Bxf6 8... Qxf6 { Retakes with the queen; ...gxf6 would tear up the pawns in front of Black's king. }
9. Nd5 9... Qd8 { The queen must leave f6. d8 keeps c7 and the knight on a5 protected. }
10. b4 10... Nxc4 { Takes the bishop first; otherwise b4 would fork the knight on a5 and the bishop on c5. }
11. bxc5 11... Na5 { The knight on c4 is attacked by the d-pawn, so it steps back to a safe square. }
12. Qd2 12... Nc6 { Back into the game. If White leaves the book, trade White's active pieces, play ...fxe4 when dxe4 opens a file for Black, and castle before you open more lines. Expect to be slightly worse. } *
